t font glyph only under the producer blank-mask guard. Writes HUD_X and target framebuffer glyph cells; preserves stage/lives and existing MMU ownership. Clobbers A/B and follows the existing render interface. Source: src/main.s and src/shared_text_runtime.inc. Current capacity and integration qualification are recorded in <a href="../tickets/bug-061-global-two-digit-part-format.html#split-formatter-fit-20261003">BUG061</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-highscore-helper-stage-player-score"><h3><code>stage_player_score</code></h3><p>BUG-069 integrated and accepted at7f52f46; parent full build and visible score handoff verified. Existing mapped stage helper paints six score digits at x33–38,row2 in light green during hidden hydration. Context2 reads current SCORE_BCD; contexts0/1 paint zero. Existing stage_panel_char preserves loop registers; score accounting and MMU ownership remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-life-marker-position"><h3><code>life_marker_position</code></h3><p>Map reserve slots0–11 to authored HUD tile roots; write HUD_X and HUD_Y only. Input A is slot0–11; A/B and condition codes are scratch. HUD origin is x33+2*(slot%3), y21−2*(slot//3). No life-counter mutation or actor-transfer ownership. Interface: <a href="#profile-render">render</a>. Source: <code>src/shared_text_runtime.inc</code>, mirrored by src/main.s and the current source-reference registry. <a href="../tickets/bug-062-twelve-life-indicator-grid.html">Approved grid contract</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-enemy-runtime-player-entry-width"><h2>player_entry_width — persistent HUD transfer width</h2><p>BUG084 helper in existing src/enemy_runtime.s. Input: INITIAL_ENTRY_STATE and hydrated current/old PLAYER_FB low byte. During WALKOUT/OFFSCREEN only, return/write PLAYER_DX=min(8,max(0,160−byte-column)); other states retain eight packed bytes. A/B/condition codes are scratch; no life-counter or framebuffer-owner mutation. Horizontal HUD rows are page-aligned. The existing persistent capture/restore/commit loops retain16 rows and eight-byte stage/save-under strides while framebuffer reads/writes use the visible width. At x320, width is zero; both owner histories must retire before normal maze entry reuses full width. Excluded nonpersistent vertical-clipping path remains unchanged. <a href="../tickets/bug-084-marker-exit-direction.html">Approved transfer contract and current evidence</a>.</section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-hud-fb-address"><h2>hud_fb_address — resolve a HUD cell framebuffer address</h2><p>Existing src/main.s render helper. Read the full-width HUD_X and HUD_Y coordinates and return X=FB_VIRT+(HUD_Y*1280)+(HUD_X*4); A/B/D and condition codes are scratch. Shared by life-marker erasure, HUD tile drawing and marker-entry setup. Interface: <a href="#profile-render">render</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-marker-entry-begin"><h2>marker_entry_begin — arm the already-consumed life</h2><p>Existing src/main.s entry-state helper; interface <a href="#profile-movement">movement</a>. Initial WAIT_STAGE consumes one reserve only after RF_STAGE commits; if the latest post-PSG status is busy, state1 and DEATH_TIMER=1 wait without repeating the decrement. Death replacement arrives after its existing decrement and uses the same wait sentinel only when prior music remains busy. On idle, read the already-decremented count as the consumed HUD slot, seed DEATH_TIMER=80 before HUD rendering mutates scratch, call life_marker_position and hud_fb_address, set DIR/face east and stateWALKOUT, and merge RF_LIVES|RF_PLAYER. A/B/D and condition codes are scratch. The accepted two-pixel WALKOUT/OFFSCREEN ticks count down the exit pad while both owner histories are checked every callback; state4 retains the Y18 final pose until the published music status is idle after the existing pending-render IRQ gate. The routine never decrements LIVES, resets maze/stage, or changes manual/want. Zero reserve